  "id": "COMPOUND:29962 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Neoisostegane may interact with BT-474, through a series of molecular targets. Neoisostegane is implicated in targeting Thioredoxin, a protein involved in cellular redox regulation and stress response. This target is further engaged by Seneciphylline and Oleiferin C, both of which are known to modulate Thioredoxin activity. The final target of this cascade is BT-474, a human breast cancer cell line, indicating a possible role in cancer progression. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Neoisostegane influences BT-474 remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway involving Thioredoxin and its downstream targets, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the therapeutic relevance and specificity of Neoisostegane in this context.",
